§ `Article 50(7): the two texts, each tested through its own function (the as-enacted dispatcher branch is dead, PLAN.md section 5), and the dispatcher on each side of 27 July 2026`

-- The text as enacted: the AI Office encourages and facilitates; the Commission may approve the codes; the Commission may specify common rules if it deems the code not adequate.
#ASSERT `Art 50(7) as enacted the official who must encourage and facilitate the drawing up of codes of practice` EQUALS `Art 50(7) the AI Office`
#ASSERT `Art 50(7) as enacted the Commission may adopt implementing acts to approve the codes of practice` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 50(7) as enacted the Commission may adopt an implementing act specifying common rules for the implementation of the obligations` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 50(7) as enacted the Commission may adopt an implementing act specifying common rules for the implementation of the obligations` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The text as amended: the Commission encourages and facilitates; it assesses adherence; the power to approve is gone; common rules if it deems the code inadequate.
#ASSERT `Art 50(7) as amended the official who must encourage and facilitate the drawing up of codes of practice` EQUALS `Art 50(7) the Commission`
#ASSERT `Art 50(7) as amended the Commission may adopt an implementing act specifying common rules for the implementation of the obligations` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 50(7) as amended the Commission may adopt an implementing act specifying common rules for the implementation of the obligations` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The dispatcher. Chapter IV applies from 2 August 2026, so on each side of 27 July 2026 it answers NOTHING (the group does not apply yet); from 2 August 2026 it gives the text as amended.
#ASSERT `Art 50(7) the official who must encourage and facilitate the drawing up of codes of practice` (Date 26 7 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 50(7) the official who must encourage and facilitate the drawing up of codes of practice` (Date 27 7 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 50(7) the official who must encourage and facilitate the drawing up of codes of practice` `Art 50 test the day before the group applies` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 50(7) the official who must encourage and facilitate the drawing up of codes of practice` `Art 50 test the first day the group applies` EQUALS JUST `Art 50(7) the Commission`
#ASSERT `Art 50(7) the Commission may adopt implementing acts to approve the codes of practice` (Date 26 7 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- 27 July 2026, the first day of the amended text: still before the group General applies (2 August 2026, Art 113), so still not covered.
#ASSERT `Art 50(7) the Commission may adopt implementing acts to approve the codes of practice` (Date 27 7 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 50(7) the Commission may adopt implementing acts to approve the codes of practice` `Art 50 test the first day the group applies` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 50(7) the Commission must assess whether adherence to the codes of practice is adequate to ensure compliance with paragraphs 2 and 4` (Date 27 7 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 50(7) the Commission must assess whether adherence to the codes of practice is adequate to ensure compliance with paragraphs 2 and 4` `Art 50 test the first day the group applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The third sentence, the dispatcher: the same answer under both texts for the same facts (the wording changed, no answer did); the date is after the group applies, so as amended.
#ASSERT `Art 50(7) the Commission may adopt an implementing act specifying common rules for the implementation of the obligations` `Art 50 test the first day the group applies` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 50(7) the Commission may adopt an implementing act specifying common rules for the implementation of the obligations` `Art 50 test the first day the group applies` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 50(7) the Commission may adopt an implementing act specifying common rules for the implementation of the obligations` (Date 26 7 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 27 July 2026: the amended text is in force and the group has not begun to apply: not covered.
#ASSERT `Art 50(7) the Commission may adopt an implementing act specifying common rules for the implementation of the obligations` (Date 27 7 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Both texts give the same answer for the same facts (shown through their own functions above): JUST TRUE if deemed inadequate, NOTHING if not.
-- The rules.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 50(7) the duty to encourage and facilitate the drawing up of codes of practice` `Art 50 test the first day the group applies` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Art 50(7) the Commission` DOES `Art 50(7) encourage and facilitate the drawing up of codes of practice at Union level` AT 2
-- No time limit and no consequence: waiting leaves the duty standing.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `Art 50(7) the duty to encourage and facilitate the drawing up of codes of practice` `Art 50 test the first day the group applies` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 400
-- Before the group applies nothing is owed.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 50(7) the duty to encourage and facilitate the drawing up of codes of practice` `Art 50 test the day before the group applies` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 400
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 50(7) the Commission's duty to assess whether adherence to the codes of practice is adequate` `Art 50 test the first day the group applies` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Art 50(7) the Commission` DOES `Art 50(7) assess whether adherence to the codes of practice is adequate` AT 5
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `Art 50(7) the Commission's duty to assess whether adherence to the codes of practice is adequate` `Art 50 test the first day the group applies` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 400

